# clamd.conf for the DocFlow pilot machine (C5.3).
#
# Copy to C:\Program Files\ClamAV\clamd.conf, then:
#   "C:\Program Files\ClamAV\clamd.exe" --install
#   Start-Service clamd
#
# DocFlow talks to clamd over a TCP socket on loopback and streams each upload
# to it (INSTREAM) before publishing. Nothing a client sends is readable by
# anyone until this service has passed it.

# The single most important line: the stock file ships with `Example` set,
# which makes clamd refuse to start. Removing it is not optional.
# Example

# --- Socket ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback only. clamd has no authentication of its own: anything that can open
# this socket can ask it to scan any file it can read.
TCPSocket 3310
TCPAddr 127.0.0.1

LogFile C:\ProgramData\ClamAV\clamd.log
LogFileMaxSize 20M
LogRotate yes
LogTime yes
PidFile C:\ProgramData\ClamAV\clamd.pid
DatabaseDirectory C:\ProgramData\ClamAV\db
TemporaryDirectory C:\ProgramData\ClamAV\tmp

# --- Limits ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app refuses anything over 25 MB before it reaches here (MAX_UPLOAD_MB).
# These are set a little above that so the scanner is never the thing that
# rejects a legitimate file — a refusal from clamd arrives as "error", which the
# app treats as "could not check", not as "bad file".
MaxFileSize 30M
MaxScanSize 60M
StreamMaxLength 30M

# Archives: a client emailing a zip of statements is normal. Ten levels is far
# past anything genuine and stops a zip bomb from occupying the scanner.
ScanArchive yes
MaxRecursion 10
MaxFiles 500

# Office documents and PDFs are what this firm actually receives.
ScanOLE2 yes
ScanPDF yes
ScanHTML yes
ScanMail no

# A file that cannot be parsed (encrypted, truncated, malformed) is reported
# rather than passed. The app already refuses encrypted PDFs and OOXML, and
# treats a scanner error as "not clean" — these two make the two layers agree.
AlertEncrypted yes
AlertBrokenExecutables yes

# --- Behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One firm's uploads are not a load problem; a couple of threads is plenty and
# leaves the machine usable as a desktop.
MaxThreads 4
MaxQueue 50
ReadTimeout 120
CommandReadTimeout 30
SelfCheck 3600

# clamd runs as the local SYSTEM account by default on Windows. It only ever
# reads from the staging directory, and DocFlow deletes the staged file itself
# once the verdict is in.
